# --- Secrets / env files ---
# Local `.env` carries `INVESTODAY_API_KEY` / `TUSHARE_TOKEN` /
# `FUND_DATA_DB` / etc. The project loader (`fund_data._env.load_env`)
# reads it at script start. SECURITY.md forbids committing these.
#
# `.env.example` is intentionally gitignored too (no allowlist):
# the project does not currently ship a template, and any template
# checked in is one copy-paste away from leaking a real key. Use
# a private `docs/secrets.md` or your shell rc to keep a template.
.env
.env.*

# --- Project artifacts ---
# Local SQLite database — generated by `fund_cli.py`. Keep schema only;
# rebuild with `python3 fund_cli.py list` after clone.
# Match any nested `data/*.sqlite` (e.g. fund-data/data/*.sqlite) too.
**/data/*.sqlite
**/data/*.sqlite-journal
**/data/*.sqlite-wal
**/data/*.sqlite-shm

# Raw offline payloads captured during local debugging.
**/data/raw_responses/
**/data/offline_*.txt
**/data/debug_*.json

# Per-user sync state and doctor dumps.
**/data/sync_state/
**/data/doctor*.txt

# Backfill runtime artifacts (large logs, incremental state).
**/data/backfill_state.json
**/data/backfill_summary.json
**/data/backfill_logs/

# OpenClaw active-completion runtime artifacts (queue JSON dumps,
# per-run execution/verification/planning outputs, lock file). The
# runner rebuilds these on every invocation; keep them out of git so
# the project state is deterministic on clone.
**/data/openclaw_runs/
**/data/openclaw_self_audit_queue.json
**/data/openclaw_self_audit_after.json
**/data/openclaw_completion_plan.json
**/data/openclaw_active_completion.lock
**/data/self_audit_queue.json
